untime", "call_id": "toolu_019pep2hnfTU8r31UD7bzk2b", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378056, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019pep2hnfTU8r31UD7bzk2b", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382080, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The problem:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the nightly test failed.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't check FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist. The fix follows what the test and docstring expect. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DoMzukWbBR8stSq7rC1nBC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GRK5YA4K67UG1CG7c9oVNB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LVcn8SDqUvf95VAGpHuMYU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015aBwXQDcNEPKbpR4XQrMkj", "caller": {"type": "dir