 "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The problem:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the nightly test failed.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't check FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist. The fix follows what the test and docstring expect. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}